Rep. Brian Poe: Your show, your time.

asr-003889
02:54:36.430 --> 02:54:37.430
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-003890
02:54:37.850 --> 02:54:40.010
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And of course, to our DICT family.

asr-003891
02:54:40.670 --> 02:54:44.270
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I remember vividly last year's budget.

asr-003892
02:54:44.630 --> 02:54:48.230
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And you, Mr. Chair, you're the one who defended their budget.

asr-003893
02:54:48.450 --> 02:54:49.270
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Diba, Mr. Chair?

asr-003894
02:54:49.550 --> 02:54:50.030
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ikaw yun eh.

asr-003895
02:54:50.030 --> 02:54:52.230
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: And the first question I asked them,

asr-003896
02:54:52.230 --> 02:54:56.910
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: how secured yung data center natin?

asr-003897
02:54:56.910 --> 02:55:05.130
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Remember, I think, no less than Secretary, when I asked during plenary budget, the hearing,

asr-003898
02:55:05.910 --> 02:55:08.590
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: sabi nyo, parang sa Florida ba?

asr-003899
02:55:09.430 --> 02:55:11.370
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: The storage of our data center?

asr-003900
02:55:11.530 --> 02:55:13.690
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Is it out of the country?

asr-003901
02:55:13.910 --> 02:55:14.450
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Tama ba yun?

asr-003902
02:55:15.510 --> 02:55:17.330
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yung data center natin, the storage?

asr-003903
02:55:19.750 --> 02:55:21.210
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Mr. Chair, Your Honor,

asr-003904
02:55:21.210 --> 02:55:22.210
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: depends po.

asr-003905
02:55:22.230 --> 02:55:26.950
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Anyway, we also have data centers that are on-prem kasama yung storage.

asr-003906
02:55:26.950 --> 02:55:36.530
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: When we're talking about the EGOV app, maybe, and a lot of the cloud storage, some of them are in Singapore and in the US naman.

asr-003907
02:55:36.530 --> 02:55:43.710
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: So merong halo na sa Pilipinas, pero mas marami po na nasa labas ng Pilipinas.

asr-003908
02:55:43.710 --> 02:55:54.500
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: I think last time, you even said that you're going to build our own storage or data facilities.

asr-003909
02:55:54.500 --> 02:55:56.020
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Here in the Philippines.

asr-003910
02:55:58.020 --> 02:55:59.000
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ongoing na ba yun?

asr-003911
02:55:59.640 --> 02:56:07.240
DICT Secretary Henry Rhoel Aguda: Mr. Chair, Your Honor, if I can ask Yusek Almirol to respond for a more accurate answer.

asr-003912
02:56:08.420 --> 02:56:12.800
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Mr. Chair, so we built the first DICT data center in Subic.

asr-003913
02:56:13.500 --> 02:56:16.100
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: So to contain only, maliit lang yun, Mr. Chair.

asr-003914
02:56:16.220 --> 02:56:18.240
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: It could only contain around 60 racks.

asr-003915
02:56:18.980 --> 02:56:23.880
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: So that's enough to use it as our archiving muna, Mr. Chair.

asr-003916
02:56:27.000 --> 02:56:30.560
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So you said 60? 60 lang yun?

asr-003917
02:56:30.820 --> 02:56:31.940
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: 60 racks lang, Mr. Chair.

asr-003918
02:56:31.960 --> 02:56:32.840
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: 6 racks. Okay.

asr-003919
02:56:33.220 --> 02:56:36.180
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So how many facilities ang kailangan natin?

asr-003920
02:56:36.420 --> 02:56:41.040
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Especially the Pax Silicae, nandun na rin.

asr-003921
02:56:41.400 --> 02:56:43.320
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So I think we need more than that.

asr-003922
02:56:45.690 --> 02:56:51.390
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Mr. Chair, according to our study, because since we have the new EO for the EO 119,

asr-003923
02:56:51.850 --> 02:56:55.130
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: the data localization as well is also being supported there.

asr-003924
02:56:55.130 --> 02:56:57.130
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: And also to simplify our...

asr-003925
02:56:57.850 --> 02:56:58.550
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Yun, nakwento ko.

asr-003926
02:56:58.570 --> 02:57:00.330
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Okay na yung copy-pasting of data, Mr. Chair.

asr-003927
02:57:00.410 --> 02:57:01.290
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Imagine yung gastos.

asr-003928
02:57:02.010 --> 02:57:03.350
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Approximately, Mr. Chair...

asr-003929
02:57:03.350 --> 02:57:04.070
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Sandali lang.

asr-003930
02:57:04.130 --> 02:57:05.950
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Mr. Chair, bakit yung oras ko umaanda?

asr-003931
02:57:06.070 --> 02:57:07.010
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Hindi naman ako nagsasalita.

asr-003932
02:57:10.690 --> 02:57:11.810
Rep. Brian Poe: Sorry, please. Go ahead.

asr-003933
02:57:14.010 --> 02:57:14.630
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Okay, Mr. Chair.

asr-003934
02:57:14.770 --> 02:57:19.210
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: So if we're going to complete that, we have a study, Mr. Chair, we can submit to you.

asr-003935
02:57:19.430 --> 02:57:21.210
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: At least around...

asr-003936
02:57:21.730 --> 02:57:27.170
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Kailangan natin, Mr. Chair, around 20 billion to really build our data sovereignty data center.

asr-003937
02:57:27.290 --> 02:57:28.830
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Na pagmamayari po ng government.

asr-003938
02:57:30.010 --> 02:57:33.090
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Going to take a look at the savings na makukuha natin,

asr-003939
02:57:33.570 --> 02:57:36.930
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: approximately, ROI natin, Mr. Chair, around 4 to 5 years then.

asr-003940
02:57:37.630 --> 02:57:39.510
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: So if we're going to localize it.

asr-003941
02:57:39.930 --> 02:57:46.070
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Kaya mas mura ang gastos, Mr. Chair, sana kung mas magandang atin yung ating mga data center

asr-003942
02:57:46.070 --> 02:57:49.990
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: instead of using foreign cloud services, Mr. Chair.

asr-003943
02:57:50.490 --> 02:57:53.710
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Right now, Mr. Chair, how much you pay for your foreign cloud services?

asr-003944
02:57:55.590 --> 02:57:59.970
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Doon sa ISSP, since we are the one chairing the MITHI together with DBM,

asr-003945
02:58:00.010 --> 02:58:06.030
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: and DEP-DEB, ang total request po of cloud subscription, Mr. Chair, is medyo malaki.

asr-003946
02:58:06.690 --> 02:58:10.530
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Umaabot po yun na mahigit 30 to 40 billion po ang request.

asr-003947
02:58:11.150 --> 02:58:15.770
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Hindi po nabibigay lahat yun, pero, Mr. Chair, ganito po kalaki yung hinihiling

asr-003948
02:58:15.770 --> 02:58:20.170
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: ng mga government agency po na dumadaan po sa ating ISSP.

asr-003949
02:58:20.370 --> 02:58:25.450
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: ISSP kasi, Mr. Chair, we are the one receiving the request of ICT plans

asr-003950
02:58:25.450 --> 02:58:27.690
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: na kailangan po ng mga government agency.

asr-003951
02:58:28.290 --> 02:58:28.970
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: So ganon po kalaki.

asr-003952
02:58:28.970 --> 02:58:29.050
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: Okay.

asr-003953
02:58:30.010 --> 02:58:34.690
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: The reason kung bakit bloated ang kakailanganin, kasi paulit-ulit yung data.

asr-003954
02:58:35.230 --> 02:58:37.290
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: We are allowing that to be bloated.

asr-003955
02:58:37.530 --> 02:58:43.110
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: But if we're able to come up with a unified data management na atin na, Mr. Chair,

asr-003956
02:58:43.650 --> 02:58:47.910
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: around estimation po namin, kasi we're conducting a feasibility study together with DBM,

asr-003957
02:58:48.390 --> 02:58:52.030
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: the savings will be around 50 to 60% savings, Mr. Chair.

asr-003958
02:58:52.610 --> 02:58:58.750
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So, in short, even though we built our own storage data center,

asr-003959
02:59:00.010 --> 02:59:02.750
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: kailangan pa rin natin mag-subscribe sa cloud.

asr-003960
02:59:04.590 --> 02:59:09.290
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: During the migration process, Mr. Chair, hindi man biglaan, but as we build our own,

asr-003961
02:59:09.570 --> 02:59:11.650
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: we do the migration little by little, Mr. Chair.

asr-003962
02:59:12.090 --> 02:59:16.910
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: And in the future, hopefully, if we already have our data sovereignty data centers,

asr-003963
02:59:17.050 --> 02:59:19.510
DICT Undersecretary David Almirol Jr.: we're able to move the majority of our data here, Mr. Chair.

asr-003964
02:59:19.510 --> 02:59:24.610
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Yeah, because I'm very serious about the hackers.

asr-003965
02:59:25.190 --> 02:59:28.130
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: So how safe are our storage data centers?

asr-003966
02:59:28.570 --> 02:59:29.310
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: How safe?

asr-003967
02:59:30.010 --> 02:59:34.250
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Ating mga documents, as far as the hacker is concerned.

asr-003968
02:59:34.390 --> 02:59:38.750
Rep. Presley C. De Jesus: Remember, DICT, you're holding the most sensitive information.

